# LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree on every platform.
#
# This is not a style preference. `bench/corpus/` is byte-exact test data
# verified by `cargo xtask corpus --check`, `spec/fixtures/` are conformance
# fixtures whose expected HTML is compared literally, and the differential
# harness (§11.2) normalises CRLF to LF on both sides because muya normalises
# to LF internally. A checkout that rewrote line endings on Windows would make
# all three subtly platform-dependent.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated fixtures: large, and not useful to read in a diff.
spec/fixtures/*.json linguist-generated=true -diff
bench/corpus/*.md linguist-generated=true -diff
